    "extraction_notes": [
      "Source PDF SHA-256: 55ee0635a83c2211a312602e2684e066f68b830f2771b6242c9a65a65827227b.",
      "P-channel polarity is preserved in tabulated signed quantities; plotted axes use the datasheet's positive magnitudes -VDS, -ID, -VGS, -VSD, and -IS.",
      "The datasheet's electrical-characteristics heading states TJ = 25 degC unless otherwise specified. Figures 1, 2, 4, and 7 do not state TJ, so their curve conditions retain TJ as not stated rather than assigning 25 degC.",
      "No transfer-characteristics ID-versus-VGS figure was published. No trr, gate resistance, or typical VSD table value was published; VSD is a maximum row value.",
      "RDS(on) table maxima are 0.032 ohm at VGS = -10 V, ID = -8 A and 0.046 ohm at VGS = -4.5 V, ID = -4 A; the schema stores the corresponding typical values.",
      "Gate-charge table values are Qg = 11.5 nC, Qgs = 3.5 nC, and Qgd = 3.3 nC under the stated VDS = -15 V, VGS = -4.5 V, ID = -1 A condition; Fig. 4 is a separate typical curve at VDS = -20 V and ID = -1 A.",
      "Curve points are manual readings from the plotted traces, retained only within the visible axes and converted to SI units.",
      "The datasheet has no explicit transfer curve, so usable_curves is true for output, RDS(on), body-diode, gate-charge, and capacitance curves, while the transfer curve is honestly omitted."
    ],
